    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Intergalactic Travel\r\n\r\nUse `intergalactic_travel_log.csv` to practice filtering and aggregating data.\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 1]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing trips that:\r\n\r\n- Have a `Class` of `\"Lux\"`\r\n- Have a non-null `PassengerName`\r\n\r\nUse AND (`&`) to combine the conditions. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 2]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing trips whose `ShipName` ends with `\"Explorer\"`. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 3]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing trips that:\r\n\r\n- Have a `Planet` of `\"Pandora\"`\r\n- Have a `Duration` greater than `6000`\r\n- Have a `TravelDate` that ends with either `\"2302\"` or `\"2303\"`\r\n\r\nUse parentheses to group the two TravelDate conditions. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 4]\r\nGroup the data by `Class`. Calculate the sum and mean of `TicketPrice` for each class. Print the summary.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [Need Help?]\r\nUse AI Tutor to look up pandas documentation, explain your filter, or request a hint. When debugging a compound filter, check what each condition returns before combining the conditions.\r\n:::",
